## Research notes

- Accessible metadata (not benchmark scores): Artificial Analysis lists Ling-3.0-flash-VL as an open-weights reasoning model (released September 2026) supporting text/image/video input and text output, with 262k-token context window, 124B total / 5.5B active parameters (MoE), and MIT license. Intelligence Index and task-level benchmark aggregates were unavailable/N/A in the fetched snapshot.
- No standalone verified benchmark scores (e.g. GPQA, SWE-bench, HLE, MMMU, Terminal-Bench, AIME, LiveCodeBench, etc.) for the exact model/ID were found in accessible sources.
